## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cablerename.html
- Summary (EN): Renames the wires of a cable through a sequence of string-replacement filters, and can append a wire index to each name with an offset.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud cablerename renomme les fils d'un câble par une suite de remplacements de chaînes, avec ajout optionnel d'un index décalé.

- Inputs meaning: ["cable: the cable whose wires are renamed"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Filters", "meaning": "Number of filters run in sequence"}, {"name": "Filter #", "meaning": "String replacement applied by that filter"}, {"name": "Use Regular Expressions", "meaning": "Switches to extended regular expressions instead of Houdini pattern syntax"}, {"name": "Replace Every Occurrence", "meaning": "Replaces all matches instead of only the first"}, {"name": "From", "meaning": "String pattern to find"}, {"name": "To", "meaning": "Replacement string"}, {"name": "Add Wire Index", "meaning": "Adds a wire index to the names"}, {"name": "Token Position", "meaning": "Places the index at the start or end of the wire name"}, {"name": "Index Offset", "meaning": "Offset applied to the wire index, which otherwise starts at 0"}]

- Caveats: ["By default only the first occurrence of a pattern is replaced", "Filters run sequentially, so their order changes the result", "Default pattern syntax follows Attribute String Edit"]

